  "safetyCrisisHeading": "You don't have to face this alone",
  "safetyCrisisBody": "If you are thinking about harming yourself, please reach out now. The help page lists crisis lines for your country.",
  "safetyUrgentHeading": "This may need urgent care",
  "safetyUrgentBody": "Chest pain, trouble breathing, fainting or a seizure need medical help now. Call your local emergency number.",
  "safetyBirthControl": "femio is not a way to avoid pregnancy and can't advise on it. A doctor, pharmacist or family-planning clinic can help you choose a method.",
  "askDiagnosisHeading": "Only a clinician can tell",
  "askDiagnosisBody": "femio can't tell whether you have a condition. A doctor can, after talking with you and, if needed, an examination or tests. Here is what trusted sources say about it.",
  "safetyHeavyBleedingHeading": "Heavy bleeding with dizziness",
  "safetyHeavyBleedingBody": "ACOG says: “If you are changing pads or tampons every hour for more than 2 hours in a row, and you also have chest pain, have shortness of breath, and are lightheaded or dizzy, seek emergency medical care right away.” If that is you, call your local emergency number now. If heavy bleeding worries you, talk to your doctor.",
  "safetyPostpartumHeading": "A warning sign after birth",
  "safetyPostpartumBody": "In the year after birth, CDC's Hear Her campaign says to get medical care immediately for an urgent warning sign, such as heavy bleeding, a fever, a headache that won't go away, a swollen leg or thoughts of harming yourself or your baby. Call your doctor or midwife now, or your local emergency number.",
