  "leaveIntro": "Your records stay on this phone: your cycle and pregnancy log, notes, health record (visits, lab results, medicines and more), documents and photos, and your birth year. femio asks your birth year to check you are 18 or over and to fit what it expects to your age. Below is every way anything can leave this phone.",
  "leaveBoostOff": "Off",
  "leaveBoostOn": "On for: {purposes}",
  "@leaveBoostOn": {
    "description": "Cloud boost status; purposes is a comma-separated list of the consented uses.",
    "placeholders": {
      "purposes": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "leaveBoostBody": "Only if you agree: a general question you approve, or four broad facts, goes to Google's cloud AI. Google Play also confirms the request comes from the real femio app.",
  "leaveModelHeading": "The on-phone AI model",
  "leaveModelBody": "If you tap Download, Android's AI service (AICore, run by Google) downloads Gemini Nano and keeps it up to date. Whenever the on-phone AI runs, Google's AI software may send Google technical usage information, such as an identifier for this installation, device and app details, errors, speed and the size of a request. It does not include your words, and femio adds none of your records to it.",
  "leavePlayHeading": "Google Play",
  "leavePlayBody": "Google Play installs and updates femio, may show its rating request, and handles femio Plus payments. It tells us only totals, such as installs and crashes. femio sends Google Play nothing of yours.",
  "leaveBackupHeading": "Your backup",
  "leaveBackupBody": "A backup, with the documents and photos you added, goes only where you choose to save it, sealed with your passphrase.",
  "leaveLinksHeading": "Links you open",
  "leaveLinksBody": "Sources and pages you open go to your browser, which visits that website.",
  "leaveNever": "Nothing else leaves. femio has no ads, no account, and no analytics or tracking tools of its own. On the phone itself, words you write for a medicine reminder show on your lock screen, and widget details you turn on show on your home screen; femio keeps that short text unencrypted so Android can show it.",
  "leaveSettingsSub": "Every way anything reaches the internet",
